From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:28:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 67/93] PCI: apple: T6050: the radio host's deep sleep where
 the sleep is described

The host registered for T6050's deep sleep on two boards by name.
Register wherever the device tree describes that sleep.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index fb2aed80ec5..fe702d2d546 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -5499,8 +5499,7 @@ static void apple_pcie_t6050_sleep_probe(struct platform_device *pdev, struct ap
 {
 	struct apple_pcie_port *port;
 
-	if (pcie->managed_sids || !(of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714s") ||
-				    of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716c")))
+	if (pcie->managed_sids || !apple_t6050_sleep_described())
 		return;
 	/* The one port a boot loader trained; an endpoint Linux powers is parked instead. */
 	list_for_each_entry(port, &pcie->ports, entry)
